{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["<b>I have given — silver of the field, take from me.</b> The word <b>נתתי</b> refers to above, where Efron said 'the field I have given to you,' and Avraham answered him: <b>hear me — I have given</b> — in astonishment. You said <b>I have given</b> it to you, but you — silver of the field, take from me; for as a gift I will not accept it. And the reason of the garesh in נתתי proves that it serves to separate it from 'silver of the field.'" "<b>[נתתי</b> — future, 'I will give,' which is like ואתן]."], :book :genesis, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 23, :notes {0 "Reading גרש as the Masoretic disjunctive accent (garesh) on נתתי, which separates it from the following words."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:05:27.921875071Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}